Host keys and power or rocker presses that don't fit the Dana's 32-report keyboard FIFO wait in order in a saved backlog of up to 8192 changes, fed into the FIFO as the guest reads reports and from CycleSlowly. Presses past that are refused, and a refused power or rocker press is logged instead of thrown. A key pressed again now waits 200 ms after its release instead of 100, as the ROM can take a press about 100 ms after the release twice.

